{{!
    @template mod_wordcards/onesided_card

    One card, showing everything at once, for learn mode when learnmodecards is set to one sided.

    Based on the cards item type in mod_minilesson. It deliberately does not carry the flip-card
    class: cardactions.js binds its click to flip handler to that class, and this card has no back
    to turn to.

    Only the term and its definition are always present. The example sentence, its translation and
    the image are each optional, and a card carrying only the first two is a normal outcome rather
    than a broken one - the model sentence translations in particular are filled in by a task on
    the dictionary server and arrive later, if at all.

    Audio needs no javascript of its own. a4e.js delegates clicks on document.body for
    ".definitions-container .definition-play-tts" and ".model-sentence-play-tts", plays
    data-modelaudio when it is a real url and falls back to speaking data-tts in data-ttsvoice, and
    stops the event propagating.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id - the term id
    * term - the word or phrase
    * definition - its definition, in the learner's definitions language
    * audio - url of recorded audio for the term, if any
    * ttsvoice - the voice to speak with when there is no recording
    * seen - whether the learner has marked this term as seen
    * image - url of an image for the term, optional. It sits with the term rather than after the
      example sentence, where a reader takes it to be a picture of the sentence
    * model_sentence - the example sentence, optional
    * model_sentence_audio - url of recorded audio for the example sentence, if any
    * model_sentence_translation - the example sentence in the learner's language, optional

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": 42,
        "term": "lantern",
        "definition": "a lamp in a case, that can be carried",
        "audio": "",
        "ttsvoice": "Amy",
        "seen": false,
        "model_sentence": "A lantern hung by the door.",
        "model_sentence_audio": "",
        "model_sentence_translation": "Un farol colgaba junto a la puerta.",
        "image": ""
    }
}}
<div class="wc-onesided-card-inner">
    {{>mod_wordcards/my_words_button}}
    <div class="term {{#seen}}term-seen{{/seen}}" data-termid="{{id}}">

        <div class="wc-onesided-term">
            <span class="wc-onesided-term-text">{{term}}</span>
            <i data-modelaudio="{{audio}}"
               data-tts="{{term}}"
               data-ttsvoice="{{ttsvoice}}"
               tabindex="0"
               role="button"
               aria-label="{{#str}}playtermaudio, mod_wordcards{{/str}}"
               class="fa fa-volume-up definition-play-tts wc-onesided-audio"></i>
        </div>

        <div class="wc-onesided-definition">{{{definition}}}</div>

        {{#image}}
        <div class="term-image term-image-{{id}}">
            <img src="{{image}}" class="flash_img wc-onesided-image" alt=""/>
        </div>
        {{/image}}

        {{#model_sentence}}
        <div class="wc-onesided-sentence">
            <span class="wc-onesided-sentence-text">{{model_sentence}}</span>
            <span data-modelaudio="{{model_sentence_audio}}"
                  data-tts="{{model_sentence}}"
                  data-ttsvoice="{{ttsvoice}}"
                  tabindex="0"
                  role="button"
                  aria-label="{{#str}}playsentenceaudio, mod_wordcards{{/str}}"
                  class="fa fa-volume-up model-sentence-play-tts wc-onesided-audio"></span>
        </div>
        {{/model_sentence}}

        {{#model_sentence_translation}}
        <div class="wc-onesided-sentence-translation">{{model_sentence_translation}}</div>
        {{/model_sentence_translation}}

    </div>
</div>
